Incident notes (from #ops-oncall)
---------------------------------
- Paged at 02:14 for a latency spike on billing-api. Traffic from the worker pool jumped 20x with
  no corresponding increase in real job volume.
- Every failing job in worker.log exhausts all 4 attempts inside about 5-6 milliseconds total.
  `backoffDelayMs(attempt, baseDelayMs)` computes 20ms / 40ms / 80ms / 160ms for baseDelayMs=10,
  but the attempts in the log are not spaced anywhere close to that - they're back-to-back.
- Config confirms `baseDelayMs` really is 10 in production, not 0. Calling `backoffDelayMs`
  directly in a REPL with those inputs returns the expected 20/40/80/160 values, so the delay
  calculation itself is not the suspect.
- Not yet root-caused. Next step is to read src/retry.ts and figure out why the computed delay
  isn't actually elapsing between attempts.
